;; A macOS sandbox profile that denies every network operation except one to
;; an address assigned to this machine. It exists for the single file of the
;; default suite that needs a listening socket:
;;
;;   corepack pnpm test:localhost
;;
;; which runs `packages/mcp-server/src/redirect.stdio.test.ts`, and nothing
;; else. Everything else runs under `tools/offline-sandbox.sb`, which denies
;; all network access and is the stronger statement.
;;
;; WHAT THIS PROFILE ALLOWS, EXACTLY
;;
;; It permits connections to addresses assigned to the current machine. That
;; includes the loopback addresses, 127.0.0.1 and ::1, AND this host's
;; local-interface addresses, such as a LAN address on en0. It is NOT
;; "loopback only", and must not be described as such: this dialect accepts
;; only `*` or `localhost` as a network-address host, where `localhost` means
;; the local host rather than 127.0.0.0/8, and it does not enforce the port,
;; so the allowance can be narrowed neither to 127.0.0.0/8 or ::1 nor to a
;; single port. The file name is historical; "local host" is the accurate
;; description.
;;
;; WHAT IT STILL DENIES
;;
;; Every host off this machine, in IPv4 and in IPv6; name resolution; and
;; UNIX-domain sockets. A subprocess inherits all of it.
;;
;; Demonstrated in the same session, under this profile, by a probe that
;; prints every outcome as observed and fails if any host off this machine is
;; reached:
;;
;;   sandbox-exec -f tools/loopback-sandbox.sb node tools/sandbox-probe.mjs
;;
;; The probe also binds and connects to a non-loopback address of this host
;; and records that it succeeds, so the allowance above is shown rather than
;; claimed. It skips that step on a host that has no non-loopback address.
;;
;; WHAT IT DOES NOT CARRY
;;
;; That the default suite needs no database. The allowance cannot exclude the
;; local PostgreSQL port, so this profile proves nothing about it. That claim
;; is carried by `tools/offline-sandbox.sb`, under which every package and
;; every file but one passes with all network denied, and by the database
;; suite being a separate command over separate files.
(version 1)
(allow default)
(deny network*)
(allow network-bind (local ip "localhost:*"))
(allow network-inbound (local ip "localhost:*"))
(allow network-outbound (remote ip "localhost:*"))
